# Menu title case

Menu bar items, menu commands, and context-menu actions use macOS title-style
capitalization (Apple HIG).

## Rules

- Capitalize the first and last word
- Capitalize nouns, pronouns, adjectives, verbs, and adverbs
- Do not capitalize articles (`a`, `an`, `the`), coordinating conjunctions
  (`and`, `or`, `but`), or short prepositions (`in`, `of`, `to`, `for`, `on`,
  `at`, `by`, `as`, …) unless they are the first or last word
- Keep the same title when the same command also appears on a toolbar or button

## Examples

| Use | Avoid |
| --- | --- |
| Show All Files in the Directory | Show all files in the directory |
| Hide Unchanged Files | Hide unchanged files |
| Copy Relative Path | Copy relative path |
| Copy Reviews | Copy reviews |
| Clear Reviews | Clear reviews |
| Copy Branch Name | Copy branch name |
| Mark as Reviewed | Mark as reviewed |
| No Recent Projects | No recent projects |

## Not menus

Field placeholders, status text, tooltips, and prose stay sentence case
(`Filter files`, `Loading…`). When Gherkin or README names a menu command,
quote the title-cased label.
